    "updated_at": "2021-09-24T07:05:00Z",
    "body": "FWIW, I'm not sure I agree with the notion that we need to define the semantics. Or at least in such a way that there is only one valid interpretation. Servers can interpret URLs however they wish and they do not necessarily need to agree with each other on that. If one server considers `a` and `A` the same and another does not, that's perfectly acceptable.",
